## 🎨 Code Style & Conventions

### TypeScript
- Use strict mode
- Define types for all API responses
- Use Zod for runtime validation (see `lib/env.ts`)

### React Components
- Use functional components with hooks
- Keep components small and focused
- Co-locate types with components

### API Routes
- Validate input with Zod schemas
- Use try-catch for error handling
- Return consistent error shapes

### Comments
- Explain WHY, not WHAT
- Reference external docs with links
- Mark evidence-based discoveries with dates

## 🧪 Testing Checklist

### Chrome Extension Testing
- [ ] Extension loads without errors
- [ ] Button appears on Lovable editor
- [ ] Button click opens iframe panel
- [ ] Project context extracted correctly
- [ ] Messages sent/received successfully
- [ ] Works after page navigation (SPA)
- [ ] No console errors

### Backend Testing (⚠️ Notify User!)
- [ ] Authentication works
- [ ] Database queries return correct data
- [ ] RLS policies enforce security
- [ ] Storage uploads succeed
- [ ] API routes handle errors gracefully

### AI Feature Testing
- [ ] AI generation completes successfully
- [ ] Correct model used
- [ ] Results are high quality
- [ ] Costs are within budget
- [ ] Rate limits not exceeded

## 🚀 Deployment

### Chrome Extension
```bash
npm run package  # Creates zip for Chrome Web Store
npm run validate # Validates manifest.json
```

### Next.js App (Lovable Production)
- Deploy via Lovable Cloud
- Set environment variables in Lovable dashboard
- Update iframe URL in `content/inject.js`

### Supabase
- ⚠️ Run migrations via MCP tools
- Verify RLS policies in production
- Test with production data (carefully!)

---

**Remember**: This is a no-code friendly project. Always explain backend operations clearly and verify with user before executing database/storage changes!

